{"sections":[],"seeAlsoSections":[{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/GettingStarted","doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/TheTurnPipeline"],"generated":true,"anchor":"Essentials","title":"Essentials"}],"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto"],["doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto","doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/BootstrapDiagnostics"],["doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto","doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/WorldMapAndExits"]]},"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"content","content":[{"anchor":"Overview","level":2,"type":"heading","text":"Overview"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A Gnusto game is one type conforming to "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/Game"},{"type":"text","text":". That one type carries everything: the rooms and things, where they start, and the rules that govern them. This article is the model underneath — how the engine finds your declarations, how one value is both a declaration and a live reference, and how the world that never changes is kept apart from the state that does."}]},{"anchor":"Declarations-are-stored-properties","level":2,"type":"heading","text":"Declarations are stored properties"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Rooms, things, and custom state are declared as "},{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"stored properties"}]},{"type":"text","text":" of the game type:"}]},{"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing","code":["struct OperaHouse: Game {","    let foyer = Location { name(\"Foyer of the Opera House\") }","    let bar   = Location { name(\"Foyer Bar\"); dark }","    let cloak = Item { name(\"velvet cloak\"); wearable }","    @Global var disturbances = 0","}"]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"When you construct the world with "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/GameWorld\/init(game:saveDirectory:)"},{"type":"text","text":", the engine’s bootstrap reflects over the game value with "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Mirror"},{"type":"text","text":" and collects every "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/Location"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/Item"},{"type":"text","text":", and "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/Global"},{"type":"text","text":". It names each entity after the property it was stored in: "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"foyer"},{"type":"text","text":" becomes "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/EntityID"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"\"foyer\""},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"cloak"},{"type":"text","text":" becomes "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"\"cloak\""},{"type":"text","text":", and so on. You never write these IDs by hand — the property name "},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"is"}]},{"type":"text","text":" the name."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"This is why declarations must live in the type’s main body, not an extension: Swift only allows stored properties there, and the Mirror only sees stored properties. (When even the declarations need to span files or ship separately, that is what a "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/GameContent"},{"type":"text","text":" bundle is for — see "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/ContentBundles"},{"type":"text","text":".)"}]},{"anchor":"One-value-two-roles","level":2,"type":"heading","text":"One value, two roles"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A declaration and a live reference are the "},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"same value"}]},{"type":"text","text":"."}]},{"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing","code":["let cloak = Item { name(\"velvet cloak\"); wearable }   \/\/ the declaration","","\/\/ …later, inside a rule body:","cloak.after(.take) {","    if cloak.isWorn { … }        \/\/ the live reference — reads current state","}"]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"cloak"},{"type":"text","text":" is an "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/Item"},{"type":"text","text":" value. Written in the game body it "},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"declares"}]},{"type":"text","text":" the cloak. Used in a rule it "},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"reads and writes the live cloak’s state"}]},{"type":"text","text":": "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/Item\/isWorn"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/Item\/isHeld"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/Item\/name"},{"type":"text","text":", and so on all consult the current turn."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"This works because each "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/Location"},{"type":"text","text":" and "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/Item"},{"type":"text","text":" mints a private identity token when it is created. The token — not the struct’s contents — is the entity’s identity, and it survives copying. Two items are equal when they share a token ("},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/Item\/==(_:_:)"},{"type":"text","text":"). Inside a turn, the token resolves to the entity’s "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/EntityID"},{"type":"text","text":" and then to its state; outside a turn there is no state to read, so a live property access traps with an explanation rather than returning a meaningless value."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"References are always compile-checked. "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"cloak.after(.take)"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"hook.holds(cloak)"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"foyer.north(bar)"},{"type":"text","text":" — every one is ordinary property access, so renaming a room or deleting an item breaks the build instead of the running game."}]},{"anchor":"The-parts-of-the-Game-protocol","level":2,"type":"heading","text":"The parts of the `Game` protocol"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/Game"},{"type":"text","text":" gathers a handful of members, most with defaults so a small game declares only what it needs:"}]},{"items":[{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"title"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"intro"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"tagline"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"maxScore"},{"type":"text","text":" — the banner and scoring metadata."}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"map"},{"type":"text","text":" — geography and initial placement, as a "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/WorldMap"},{"type":"text","text":". Read once at startup to build the initial state."}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"rules"},{"type":"text","text":" — all game logic, as a "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/Rules"},{"type":"text","text":" value. Defaults to empty."}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"verbs"},{"type":"text","text":" — player-typeable verbs this game adds, as "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"[SyntaxRule]"},{"type":"text","text":". Defaults to empty. See "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/AddingCustomVerbs"},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"content"},{"type":"text","text":" — content bundles the game composes itself from, as "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/GameContents"},{"type":"text","text":". Defaults to empty. See "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/ContentBundles"},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"type":"paragraph"}]}],"type":"unorderedList"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The protocol extension also hands every game three ambient references usable as bare identifiers inside "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"map"},{"type":"text","text":" and "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"rules"},{"type":"text","text":" blocks:"}]},{"items":[{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"player"},{"type":"text","text":" — the "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/Player"},{"type":"text","text":", for its location, score, and inventory, and "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/Player\/item"},{"type":"text","text":" for the player as a thing in the world (what "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"X ME"},{"type":"text","text":" examines)."}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"world"},{"type":"text","text":" — the "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/World"},{"type":"text","text":", for rules that apply everywhere (like daemons)."}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"command"},{"type":"text","text":" — the "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/Command"},{"type":"text","text":" currently being performed, inside a rule body."}],"type":"paragraph"}]}],"type":"unorderedList"},{"anchor":"The-map-block","level":2,"type":"heading","text":"The `map` block"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"map"},{"type":"text","text":" is a result-builder property that yields a "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/WorldMap"},{"type":"text","text":" — a flat list of "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/MapEntry"},{"type":"text","text":" statements: exits, initial item placements, and the player’s start."}]},{"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing","code":["var map: WorldMap {","    foyer.south(bar)                 \/\/ an exit","    bar.north(foyer)                 \/\/ and the way back, stated separately","","    player.starts(in: foyer)         \/\/ where the player begins","    cloak.startsWorn                 \/\/ where each thing begins","}"]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Exits are one-way, so an asymmetric map needs no special case. There are five kinds of exit and eight ways to place a thing; "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/WorldMapAndExits"},{"type":"text","text":" covers all of them."}]},{"anchor":"Immutable-definition-mutable-state","level":2,"type":"heading","text":"Immutable definition, mutable state"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Internally, the engine keeps two things strictly apart:"}]},{"items":[{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The "},{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"text":"definition","type":"text"}]},{"type":"text","text":" is everything that never changes during play: names, descriptions, exits, rules, and the parser’s vocabulary. It is built once, from your declarations, at startup."}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The "},{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"text":"state","type":"text"}]},{"type":"text","text":" is everything that "},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"text":"does","type":"text"}]},{"type":"text","text":" change: where each item is, what is lit, the score, the turn count, which things have been touched, and your "},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/Global"},{"text":" values.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]}],"type":"unorderedList"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The entire mutable state is a single "},{"code":"Codable","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" value. Every change funnels through it, so a turn commits atomically at its end (see "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/TheTurnPipeline","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":") and save\/restore is a serialization call rather than a feature threaded through the codebase."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"When you write ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"cloak.isWorn"},{"text":" or ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"player.score += 1"},{"text":" in a rule, you are reading and writing that one state value through the entity’s token — never touching the definition, and never seeing another turn’s half-finished changes.","type":"text"}]},{"anchor":"See-also","level":2,"type":"heading","text":"See also"},{"type":"unorderedList","items":[{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/GettingStarted","isActive":true,"ty